[ti:A Clearer Route to PyTorch Certification]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: You know some Python. You've studied machine learning.
[00:00.00]Ava：你懂一些 Python，也学过机器学习。
[00:03.61]Now you're learning PyTorch, and you'd like a clear target.
[00:03.61]现在你开始学 PyTorch，想有个明确目标。
[00:07.55]What should you actually learn before trying to prove you can use it?
[00:07.55]在证明自己会用它之前，究竟该学些什么？
[00:12.52]Brian: That's the problem this article addresses.
[00:12.52]Brian：这正是这篇文章要回答的问题。
[00:15.55]It introduces a learning pathway for the PyTorch Certified Associate, or PTCA, certification.
[00:15.55]文章介绍了一条备考 PyTorch Certified Associate（PTCA）认证的学习路径。
[00:22.28]It brings focused learning and the certification exam together in one structured experience.
[00:22.28]它把有针对性的学习和认证考试整合成一套有条理的课程。
[00:29.28]Ava: I'm Ava, a software engineer outside the PyTorch core team.
[00:29.28]Ava：我是 Ava，一名不在 PyTorch 核心团队的软件工程师。
[00:33.88]Brian, you're here to walk us through it.
[00:33.88]Brian，今天请你带我们了解一下。
[00:37.08]Is the main news a new exam, or a new way to prepare?
[00:37.08]这次的主要消息是新考试，还是新的备考方式？
[00:41.56]Brian: The announcement is about the new Certification Pathway.
[00:41.56]Brian：这次发布的是新的认证学习路径。
[00:45.37]It's offered through Linux Foundation Education, and it combines four self-paced learning modules with the PTCA certification exam.
[00:45.37]它由 Linux Foundation Education 提供，包含四个自主安排进度的学习模块和 PTCA 认证考试。
[00:54.63]Ava: Okay, so the learning and the exam come in one product.
[00:54.63]Ava：明白了，学习和考试打包在一起。
[00:58.06]But putting them together wouldn't automatically make the learning useful.
[00:58.06]但放在一起，不代表课程自然就有用。
[01:02.67]What's the connection between the course material and the certification?
[01:02.67]课程内容和认证有什么联系？
[01:07.51]Brian: The article says the learning more closely aligns with the certification's domains and competencies.
[01:07.51]Brian：文章说，课程内容与认证考查的领域和能力更加一致。
[01:13.80]In plain English, those are the areas it covers and the skills you're expected to understand.
[01:13.80]说白了，就是考试覆盖的内容，以及你需要掌握的技能。
[01:20.00]Ava: It's like having a map with the destination marked.
[01:20.00]Ava：就像拿到一张标出了目的地的地图。
[01:23.06]You still have to make the trip, but at least the road and the destination belong on the same map.
[01:23.06]路还得自己走，但至少路线和目的地在同一张地图上。
[01:29.28]Brian: Right. That's a useful way to think about the structure.
[01:29.28]Brian：对，这样理解它的安排很贴切。
[01:33.33]The modules cover the same key areas measured by PTCA, with learning and hands-on labs along the way.
[01:33.33]这些模块涵盖 PTCA 考查的关键领域，途中还有学习内容和动手实验。
[01:40.98]Ava: Before we open that map, who's it for?
[01:40.98]Ava：看这张地图之前，先说说它适合谁？
[01:43.59]Our listeners may already work on deep-learning frameworks.
[01:43.59]我们的听众可能已经在研究深度学习框架。
[01:47.63]Some will be comfortable with ideas that a beginner hasn't met yet.
[01:47.63]有些人熟悉的概念，初学者可能还没接触过。
[01:52.57]Brian: PTCA is designed for early-stage practitioners who have Python and machine learning experience and are beginning to work with PyTorch.
[01:52.57]Brian：PTCA 面向有 Python 和机器学习经验、刚开始使用 PyTorch 的入门阶段从业者。
[02:01.49]That's the audience the article explicitly names.
[02:01.49]这是文章明确指出的目标人群。
[02:05.11]Ava: So we shouldn't describe it as starting from absolutely zero.
[02:05.11]Ava：所以不能说它是从零开始。
[02:09.03]There's already some programming and machine learning background in the picture.
[02:09.03]学习者需要有一定的编程和机器学习基础。
[02:14.17]The new ground is working with PyTorch.
[02:14.17]新要学的是使用 PyTorch。
[02:17.03]Brian: Exactly. And the stated aim is a strong foundation.
[02:17.03]Brian：没错。它的目标是打下扎实的基础。
[02:20.73]For an experienced framework engineer listening today, that helps set expectations about the level of this announcement.
[02:20.73]对有经验的框架工程师来说，这也说明了这次发布内容的定位。
[02:29.78]Ava: Let's walk through the learning. Four modules sounds manageable as a structure.
[02:29.78]Ava：来看看课程安排。四个模块，结构上挺清晰。
[02:34.84]What are their names, and how do they connect to the work of building a model?
[02:34.84]它们分别叫什么？又怎样对应模型开发工作？
[02:40.19]Brian: They're PyTorch Fundamentals, Data Handling in PyTorch, PyTorch Model Development, and Optimizing PyTorch.
[02:40.19]Brian：分别是 PyTorch Fundamentals（PyTorch 基础）、Data Handling in PyTorch（PyTorch 数据处理）、PyTorch Model Development（PyTorch 模型开发）和 Optimizing PyTorch（PyTorch 优化）。
[02:47.58]Together, they cover core skills from working with tensors and devices through improving model performance.
[02:47.58]它们涵盖从张量、设备操作到提升模型性能的核心技能。
[02:55.40]Ava: Let's unpack tensors and devices briefly.
[02:55.40]Ava：简单说说张量和设备吧。
[02:58.42]Think of tensors as containers of numerical data, and devices as where computation happens.
[02:58.42]可以把张量看作数值数据的容器，设备则是执行计算的地方。
[03:05.14]What does the article say learners will do with them?
[03:05.14]文章说学员会用它们做什么？
[03:09.40]Brian: They'll work with tensors and devices across the model lifecycle.
[03:09.40]Brian：他们会在模型的整个生命周期中使用张量和设备。
[03:13.59]That's the span of working with a model, which the article describes here as going from training through prediction.
[03:13.59]这里的模型生命周期，文章描述为从训练到预测的全过程。
[03:21.42]Ava: That gives the fundamentals a purpose.
[03:21.42]Ava：这样，基础知识就有了实际用途。
[03:24.03]You're following those concepts through actual model work.
[03:24.03]你会在实际的模型工作中用到这些概念。
[03:28.03]Does the post explain individual exercises, or show what a learner builds?
[03:28.03]文章有介绍具体练习，或展示学员会做出什么吗？
[03:33.48]Brian: It doesn't give that level of detail.
[03:33.48]Brian：没有讲得那么细。
[03:36.14]It names the skills and says there are hands-on labs.
[03:36.14]它列出了要学的技能，也说有动手实验。
[03:39.96]We don't get an exercise list or a sample project.
[03:39.96]但没有练习清单或示例项目。
[03:43.91]Ava: Fair enough. Next comes data handling.
[03:43.91]Ava：明白。接下来是数据处理。
[03:46.61]That's a familiar part of the workflow for our audience, but the PyTorch names may still be new to some listeners.
[03:46.61]我们的听众熟悉这部分流程，但有些人可能还不熟悉 PyTorch 里的这些名称。
[03:55.08]Brian: The pathway covers preparing and managing data using Datasets, DataLoaders, and transforms.
[03:55.08]Brian：这条学习路径涵盖如何用 Datasets、DataLoaders 和 transforms 准备、管理数据。
[04:01.83]Those are the named tools for this part of the learning.
[04:01.83]这就是课程在数据处理部分提到的工具。
[04:06.33]Ava: For anyone hearing those names for the first time, could we give them a simple picture?
[04:06.33]Ava：能给第一次听到这些名称的朋友简单解释一下吗？
[04:12.09]Three unfamiliar terms in one sentence can feel like a small vocabulary exam.
[04:12.09]一句话里出现三个陌生术语，感觉像在做一场小型词汇测验。
[04:17.55]Brian: Think of organizing your material, bringing it into the workflow, and applying changes to it.
[04:17.55]Brian：可以把它理解为整理材料、将其送入工作流程，再对其进行处理。
[04:24.17]That's a rough picture of Datasets, DataLoaders, and transforms.
[04:24.17]这大致就是 Datasets、DataLoaders 和 transforms 的作用。
[04:28.72]The post doesn't explain their mechanics.
[04:28.72]文章没有解释它们的具体工作机制。
[04:31.99]Ava: Got it. The point to remember is preparing and managing data.
[04:31.99]Ava：明白了。要记住的重点是准备和管理数据。
[04:36.38]Then we reach model development.
[04:36.38]接下来是模型开发。
[04:38.68]What building blocks does the article actually name there?
[04:38.68]文章在这部分具体提到了哪些基础组件？
[04:43.21]Brian: It names PyTorch layers, activations, loss functions, and optimizers for building neural networks.
[04:43.21]Brian：文章提到了用于构建神经网络的 PyTorch 层、激活函数、损失函数和优化器。
[04:49.90]In broad terms, that's model structure, how signals change, how errors are measured, and how learning is guided.
[04:49.90]概括来说，就是模型结构、信号如何变化、如何衡量误差，以及如何引导学习。
[04:57.89]Ava: That vocabulary will be familiar to someone with machine learning experience.
[04:57.89]Ava：有机器学习经验的人应该熟悉这些术语。
[05:03.05]The pathway gives those ideas a PyTorch setting.
[05:03.05]这条学习路径把这些概念放进了 PyTorch 的语境。
